exports[`phone skills given: [case8] the --help of each other phone skill when: [t0] each runs with --help then: the usages match their snapshot 1`] = `
"🪨 run solid skill repo=bhuild/role=dispatcher/skill=phone.contacts

🦫 here's who you may reach

💧 phone.contacts --help
   ├─ usage
   │  ├─ phone.contacts get                       this clone's contacts + own tree, with reach state
   │  ├─ phone.contacts set --address <address>   grant; idempotent
   │  └─ phone.contacts del --address <address>   revoke; idempotent
   │
   └─ set and del need a human, or a clone whose meter is allowed: rhx phone.contacts.uses get
---
🪨 run solid skill repo=bhuild/role=dispatcher/skill=phone.contacts.uses

🦫 here's the dam

💧 phone.contacts.uses --help
   ├─ usage
   │  ├─ phone.contacts.uses get     may this tree's clones manage their own contacts?
   │  ├─ phone.contacts.uses allow   lift the meter (human only)
   │  └─ phone.contacts.uses block   drop the meter (human only)
   │
   └─ blocked by default; unset reads as blocked
---
🪨 run solid skill repo=bhuild/role=dispatcher/skill=phone.daemon

🦫 here's the daemon

💧 phone.daemon --help
   └─ usage
      ├─ phone.daemon get   is a daemon live in this tree?
      ├─ phone.daemon set   find the live daemon, or start one
      └─ phone.daemon del   stop it; no text is lost"
`;

exports[`phone skills given: [case9] a mechanic and a foreman in one tree, on a stub rhachet when: [t0] the mechanic texts the foreman, and the foreman replies then: every output and every said message matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"🪨 run solid skill repo=bhuild/role=dispatcher/skill=phone.text

🦫 tail slapped!

💧 phone.text set
   ├─ from: phone://grove=bert-laptop/tree=$TREE/clone=mechanic
   ├─ to: phone://grove=bert-laptop/tree=$TREE/clone=foreman
   ├─ text: <text>
   ├─ 1 repeated --to dropped; each peer gets one text
   └─ status: QUEUED → a daemon started (was down); it delivers it
---
🪨 run solid skill repo=bhuild/role=dispatcher/skill=phone.text

🦫 here's the thread

💧 phone.text get
   └─ <text> ← phone://grove=bert-laptop/tree=$TREE/clone=mechanic   DELIVERED
      ├─ slot shape changed for book-a-lesson
      └─ it's 'lesson.slot', not 'slot'
---
🪨 run solid skill repo=bhuild/role=dispatcher/skill=phone.text

🦫 tail slapped!

💧 phone.text set
   ├─ from: phone://grove=bert-laptop/tree=$TREE/clone=foreman
   ├─ to: phone://grove=bert-laptop/tree=$TREE/clone=mechanic
   ├─ text: <text>, re <text>
   └─ status: QUEUED → the daemon delivers it
---
🪨 run solid skill repo=bhuild/role=dispatcher/skill=phone.text

🦫 here's the thread

💧 phone.text get
   ├─ <text> → phone://grove=bert-laptop/tree=$TREE/clone=foreman   DELIVERED
   │  ├─ slot shape changed for book-a-lesson
   │  └─ it's 'lesson.slot', not 'slot'
   └─ <text> ← phone://grove=bert-laptop/tree=$TREE/clone=foreman   DELIVERED · re <text>
      └─ got it; slot renamed
---
🦫🔔 text <text> from phone://grove=bert-laptop/tree=$TREE/clone=mechanic

slot shape changed for book-a-lesson
it's 'lesson.slot', not 'slot'

   └─ reply
      ├─ rhx phone.text set --to phone://grove=bert-laptop/tree=$TREE/clone=mechanic --re <text> --what '...'
      └─ words with quotes or newlines? pipe them in: --what @stdin
---
🦫🔔 text <text> from phone://grove=bert-laptop/tree=$TREE/clone=foreman (re <text>)

got it; slot renamed

   └─ reply
      ├─ rhx phone.text set --to phone://grove=bert-laptop/tree=$TREE/clone=foreman --re <text> --what '...'
      └─ words with quotes or newlines? pipe them in: --what @stdin"
`;

